## Data boundaries

- **Canonical dataset:** `data/releases/` (CC BY 4.0) — prefer
  `yarn structure-hromada … --write-release`
- **Provenance only:** `data/research-log/` — dated snapshots, not maintained dataset
- **Not public:** `internal/` — outreach drafts (`outreach-messages.md`;
  optional convenience HTML `internal/outreach.html` is gitignored and must
  not be published under `docs/`).
- **Local source caches (gitignored):** `scripts/retrieval/raw/` (strategy PDFs) via `yarn download-raw`; `data/cache/mss/` (МСС registry XLSX) via `yarn fetch-mss-registry`; `data/cache/twinning/` (SKEW HTML) via `yarn twinning` — for re-analysis, not the release
- **KSE covariates:** fetch at analysis time via `enrich_from_kse.py`; do not vendor KSE CSVs
- **Archived (do not run day-to-day):** `scripts/analysis/legacy/` (early matching
  passes); `scripts/legacy/nocodb/` (former shared CRM sync)

## Matching pipeline (current)

`yarn match` → `scripts/analysis/match.py` v7.3:
`0.60 × priority + 0.25 × geo + 0.15 × social_capital`

`priority` is Goals cosine when both sides have strategy text (plus **0.10 ×
DREAM title cosine** if both also have DREAM projects). When a side has no
Goals, DREAM project titles fill that same 0.60 slot (0.90×, mixed or
`dream_proxy`). `social_capital` is readiness / social capital: KSE/Пліч
`mss_network` is the floor; named neighbour / explicit-ask, **both-sides**
registry UA–EU twinning, and shared donor programmes add at lower weight (capped at 1.0).
One-sided twinning is not a pair signal. Never `known: true` from those extras.
After changes, run `yarn test-length-norm`,
`yarn test-known-pairs`, `yarn test-social-capital`, `yarn test-dream-proxy`,
`yarn test-afccre-twinning` when touching the FR jumelage layer,
and `yarn report-pin-corpus`.

Still separate (do **not** fold into combined `score`):
- `yarn complementary-match` — resource/DREAM ↔ Challenges (asymmetric;
  v3 kitchen-sink sectors capped; named deficit↔offer; this is «навіщо»,
  not trust). Different from DREAM-title *similarity*.
- `yarn extract-strategy-entities` — named objects + GISRR SWOT/task extras;
  shared-asset overlay. Neighbour NER feeds `social_capital` named (0.70)
  via explicit-ask, not the 0.60 Goals slot.
- HydroBASINS / `same_basin` — map underlay only
- `yarn hromada-resources` / `yarn fetch-dream` — structural covariates
  (`dream_overlap` stays on operational_score)

PIN map (`yarn graph-pin-matching`): paint **thematic**, **operational**,
**complementary**, **explicit_ask**, and **shared_asset** overlays separately —
never top-N by combined `score` (sparse corpus → geo bias). **Twinning** stays a node highlight
layer (EU sister cities in the hromada card + indigo glow) *and* a weak
pairwise input to `social_capital`. **SKEW = DE registry; AFCCRE = FR
registry** (PDF jumelage directory, `yarn twinning`, 2026-09-17: 63 raw →
56 linked / 7 skipped; never `known: true`). Ministry FR rows that match
AFCCRE are tagged `duplicate_of_afccre`. Skip Kyiv city/districts and Crimea
Yalta. MEAE Atlas was not scrapeable. **Interreg** (keep.eu LPA) is a separate
cyan node highlight; official keep.eu `themes[]` also feed the «Теми UA–ЄС»
filter. **Law 3668-IX** registered international agreements feed the card +
that same filter + a revealed EU-place pool — not v7 `score`,
never `known: true`, never Law 1508 forms.

**3668 snapshot (2026-09-16):** 312 filled rows → **197 matched / 107
hromadas** (7% of 1463); 41 oblast skipped, 74 unmatched. PL 164/312 then
RO 52, MD 27 (78% together). Lviv+Volyn+Chernivtsi = 129 agreements.
Culture on 142/197 is kitchen-sink sphere text, not specialization; 27
untagged. 2025 spike (57) includes Bucharest 19.11.2025 Chernivtsi↔RO pack
and Kyiv 06.06.2025 batch; **2024 = 0**. Of 107: 72 also twinning, 11 also
Interreg LPA (themes rarely overlap), 31 only 3668. Stem collision:
Миколаївська city swallowed Lviv-oblast gmina deals — check title, not only
KATOTTG. Incomplete vs Ministry ~2119 dashboard. Western PL/RO corridor,
not a distant-EU twin finder. Analytics canvas:
`canvases/law-3668-agreements.canvas.tsx` (Cursor canvases folder).

**EU–EU IMC briefing (2026-09-18):** how EU municipalities cooperate *with
each other* — three stacks to keep apart from UA layers. (1) Domestic IMC
under 27 national laws (bulk: water/waste/fire/back-office). France EPCI =
mandatory coverage (1 252 on 1.1.2026), not a partner-search market; Poland
`związki` is the closest legal cousin of Law 1508. No EU-wide IMC registry.
(2) Cross-border: Madrid Convention → Euroregion → EGTC (~86 active; CoR
93 listed / 7 closed) → Interreg project (€8.05 bn 2021–27, 72% internal
CBC). EGTC ≠ grant. keep.eu still needs `Local public authority` filter.
(3) Soft: CEMR twinning last census 2010 ~34k; LEADER ~2 678 LAGs. Same
product discipline as SKEW: never `known: true`, never v7 `score`. Full
EU↔EU matching stays Phase 3. Write-up: [docs/eu-imc.md](../../docs/eu-imc.md).
Canvas: `canvases/eu-imc.canvas.tsx`.

## Hard rules

1. Matching scores are **hypotheses** unless `known: true` (curated registry-confirmed). Do not set `known: true` on all PIN edges — use `matching-edges.pin-corpus.json` for the broader overlap. Do not set `known: true` on twinning links either (SKEW / AFCCRE are foreign twinning, not domestic МСС).
2. Sector-tag overlap is **not** a matching signal.
3. `edem_total`: use `edem-data.csv`; missing hromadas ≠ zero.
4. Batch growth: `scripts/retrieval/` + in-session structuring → `yarn structure-hromada --json … --write-release`. Prefer `yarn priority-corpus-growth` when expanding PIN∩corpus validation coverage. See [docs/corpus-growth.md](../../docs/corpus-growth.md).
5. Do not inflate CKAN "123 strategies" — mostly unrelated datasets.
6. Minimize scope; match existing TS/Python conventions in `scripts/`.
7. Product unit is an **МСС candidate agreement** (`package` theme·form +
   `signals[]`). Do not present combined `score` as «strategy match». Signal
   labels (`схожа стратегія` / `зручний сусід` / `доповнення` / `явний запит` /
   `спільний обʼєкт` / `місто-побратим ЄС` / `схожі проєкти DREAM`) are discovery evidence — **not** the five legal IMC forms.
   Browse by hypothesis strength; form filter is secondary (do not primary-nav by
   form buckets — most suggestions default to спільний проєкт).
8. `suggested_theme` / `suggested_form` / `package` are IMC-package hypotheses
   (`mss_suggest.py` → `mss_candidate.py`) — never fold into `score`, never set
   `known: true` from them. UI atom: human `package.label_uk` + 1–3 signal chips.
9. **Trust / benefit (Tkachuk):** do not claim the tool replaces personal
   relations between heads. Surface clear «навіщо» (budget savings, revenue,
   image, joint grant). Motivation > venue. Wartime thematic priorities drift
   (water → energy → winter infra) — do not freeze one eternal thematic prior.
   **Frozen local elections (2020→):** *sticky heads* now (network discovery
   stronger); *fragile heads* after future elections — prefer packages that
   survive a change of person. See
   [mss-cooperation-research.md#frozen-elections-otg](../../docs/mss-cooperation-research.md#frozen-elections-otg).
10. **HydroBASINS / water:** map underlay + `same_basin` context only — never
    fold into v7 `score`, never `known: true`. Water-theme IMC ≠ basin
    hydrology; keep them distinct (see `docs/external-data-sources.md`).

